1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:03,220
Responder is the personal
workspace for a named member.

2
00:00:03,619 --> 00:00:08,989
Check the account and department, then
read My Status and My Staffing on Home.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,260
People, Units, and Calls provide
the wider operating picture.

4
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:18,190
A community response team can use the
same pattern to show who is available and

5
00:00:18,190 --> 00:00:20,120
which incident each person is joining.

6
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:24,540
Every name and incident shown here belongs
to our fictional training department.

7
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:28,810
First launch introduces Resgrid
Responder, Instant Notifications,

8
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:30,500
and Interact with Calls.

9
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:35,829
Use Next to read each page, Skip
to leave the introduction, or Let’s

10
00:00:35,829 --> 00:00:37,520
Get Started on the final page.

11
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:40,100
Language is available on the login screen.

12
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:45,349
These introduction pages describe intended
features; they do not establish that this

13
00:00:45,349 --> 00:00:50,140
browser has received a push notification
or exercised a native device permission.

14
00:00:50,349 --> 00:00:54,519
Use Change Server URL before
signing in when your organization

15
00:00:54,519 --> 00:00:56,589
supplies a different API endpoint.

16
00:00:57,080 --> 00:01:02,210
The Server selector offers regional
choices and Custom; Server URL takes

17
00:01:02,210 --> 00:01:07,459
the API origin without slash api
slash v four or a trailing slash.

18
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:11,039
This recording uses only
the local fictional API.

19
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:16,389
Return to Username and Password, then
Login using your own authorized account.

20
00:01:16,729 --> 00:01:19,990
Keep credentials outside
screenshots and shared recordings.

21
00:01:20,189 --> 00:01:25,000
Login with SSO opens a separate entry
screen with Username or Email and

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,899
Department ID, which is optional.

23
00:01:27,449 --> 00:01:31,109
Continue starts the organization’s
configured identity flow.

24
00:01:31,569 --> 00:01:35,210
The training environment has no
usable identity-provider discovery

25
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:38,700
configuration, so this is an
entry-screen walkthrough only.

26
00:01:39,139 --> 00:01:44,030
A deployed organization must verify its
provider, return link, and any additional

27
00:01:44,030 --> 00:01:48,059
challenge on the intended platform
before relying on that sign-in path.

28
00:01:48,199 --> 00:01:51,949
Recover your account explains that
a recovery code is entered after a

29
00:01:51,949 --> 00:01:53,969
password or organization sign-in.

30
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:59,170
Without that code, contact the department
administrator or support; this screen

31
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:01,590
cannot turn off two-factor authentication.

32
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:04,979
Back to sign in returns
to the normal entry point.

33
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:09,379
We are showing the actual no-challenge
view, without changing credentials,

34
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:13,299
creating recovery codes, or claiming
that verification has completed.

35
00:02:13,519 --> 00:02:17,279
On Home, select Status and
read the offered choices before

36
00:02:17,279 --> 00:02:18,729
changing your personal state.

37
00:02:19,130 --> 00:02:24,339
This department offers Responding, Not
Responding, On Scene, and Standing By.

38
00:02:24,809 --> 00:02:27,969
Its labels and transitions come
from department configuration.

39
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:32,640
The example selects Responding
and opens Set Status: Responding.

40
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:37,640
After the completed action, My Status
shows the saved state and destination.

41
00:02:37,999 --> 00:02:40,429
Use the displayed result
to confirm the change.

42
00:02:40,650 --> 00:02:44,460
The destination step separates
Calls, Stations, and POI.

43
00:02:45,139 --> 00:02:48,570
Select the intended destination
before moving to Add Note.

44
00:02:49,039 --> 00:02:53,599
In this exercise, the community medical
standby is the chosen call and the note

45
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:56,080
clearly says it is an Academy exercise.

46
00:02:56,539 --> 00:02:59,379
Save completes the personal
status change, and the Home

47
00:02:59,379 --> 00:03:01,049
card displays that destination.

48
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:05,459
Read any required-field instruction in
your department rather than assuming

49
00:03:05,490 --> 00:03:07,709
every status uses the same steps.

50
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,590
Staffing records your
availability for assignment.

51
00:03:10,959 --> 00:03:16,579
This department offers Available, Delayed,
Unavailable, Committed, and On Shift.

52
00:03:16,970 --> 00:03:20,900
The example chooses Available,
uses Add Note to state the training

53
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:24,690
availability window, and checks
Review and Confirm before Submit.

54
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:27,440
My Staffing then shows the saved result.

55
00:03:27,909 --> 00:03:32,020
Personal status and staffing serve
different coordination needs, so read

56
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:36,040
both cards when handing over a community
care or search-team duty period.

57
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:41,430
People shows the member’s group, role,
status, staffing, and update time.

58
00:03:41,919 --> 00:03:46,660
Search personnel and Filter Personnel
narrow that picture by Groups and Roles.

59
00:03:47,130 --> 00:03:50,609
Units has its own search and
opens resource details such as

60
00:03:50,609 --> 00:03:52,520
Location and Vehicle Information.

61
00:03:52,850 --> 00:03:56,420
These are useful reference views for
a search-and-rescue team, security

62
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:58,280
patrol, or industrial standby.

63
00:03:58,819 --> 00:04:03,100
Reading a unit here does not establish
an active shared-device crew session.

64
00:04:03,359 --> 00:04:07,510
Open Sign-in and security to review
Authenticator app, Passkeys for

65
00:04:07,510 --> 00:04:09,990
this app, and Recent verifications.

66
00:04:10,479 --> 00:04:14,210
The actual training account says
its authenticator is not set up,

67
00:04:14,399 --> 00:04:18,840
has no app passkeys, and has no
verifications in the last thirty days.

68
00:04:19,250 --> 00:04:23,300
Those are configuration states, not
proof of a successful challenge.

69
00:04:23,689 --> 00:04:27,780
Setup or credential changes belong to
the organization’s approved security

70
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:30,339
process and are outside this exercise.

71
00:04:30,530 --> 00:04:34,450
Responder approvals lists device
approval availability; this

72
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:36,300
account shows Approvals stopped.

73
00:04:36,809 --> 00:04:40,860
A configured approval request must be
matched to a sign-in you initiated,

74
00:04:41,059 --> 00:04:43,589
including its number, before any approval.

75
00:04:44,009 --> 00:04:47,230
No challenge or hardware
notification was exercised here.

76
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:51,689
For a shared or handed-over device,
Logout asks for confirmation

77
00:04:51,689 --> 00:04:53,629
before clearing local session data.

78
00:04:54,039 --> 00:04:57,520
The declared web recording adapter
preserves the source confirmation

79
00:04:57,520 --> 00:05:01,219
text and buttons; native confirmation
remains platform-specific.
